{"clips": [
  {
    "id": "C1",
    "weakest_point": "Between 4.5s and 9.3s the scene slows to a series of glaring close-ups and talk; a scroller who didn’t buy the theft premise in the first second could drop before Gerald enters with the riding crop.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "At 1.1s Juliana shouts \"No! That watch was not in his coat!\" while physically shielding Alexander from the Constable’s outstretched handcuffs—immediate, context-free conflict with clear stakes."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Ends on Clarissa’s cruel demand \"I want to see you crawl, sister,\" which is a strong villain peak, but it is less specific and urgent than a life-or-death ultimatum."
    },
    "questions": [
      {"q": "Will Juliana agree to Clarissa’s cruel demand to save Alexander?", "type": "intrigue"},
      {"q": "Did Gerald really plant the watch?", "type": "intrigue"}
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "Zero context needed: a wife physically blocks police from arresting her husband over a planted watch, while a sister and a constable gloat."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Strong sense of injustice and family betrayal; Clarissa’s line \"still defending your broken scrap of a man?\" is viscerally cruel."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The cruel demand makes you want to see Juliana’s response, though the exact stakes of \"crawl\" are not yet spelled out."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Verbal threats and handcuffs only; no physical violence, blood, or sexual content is shown."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "A clean, context-free opening that establishes the frame-up instantly, though it ends on a slightly softer villain beat than C2."
  },
  {
    "id": "C2",
    "weakest_point": "The first 3 seconds drop you mid-argument with Gerald pointing a crop; without C1’s opening \"No!\", a cold scroller may not know who is wronged or why.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Gerald’s line \"Then perhaps your wife should explain why it was found in your coat\" is intriguing but assumes you already know the characters and the theft setup."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "Cuts on the whispered ultimatum \"Fail, or refuse, and your husband hangs from the gallows\"—a specific, burning question with the highest possible stakes."
    },
    "questions": [
      {"q": "Will Juliana risk shredding her hands in the frozen briars?", "type": "intrigue"},
      {"q": "Can she retrieve the ring before the magistrate arrives?", "type": "intrigue"}
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The title and actions make the marriage and frame-up clear, but the opening line presumes knowledge of the watch accusation."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "The ultimatum is a gut punch—cruel, specific, and terrifying; the sadistic task design (\"A lady’s hands will be shredded to ribbons!\") amplifies the injustice."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 5,
      "reason": "The gallows threat and bare-handed retrieval demand are impossible to ignore."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Threats of hanging and shredded hands are verbal only; no violence is shown on screen."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "The sharpest cliffhanger of the three, but it sacrifices the cold-open hook by starting mid-conversation."
  },
  {
    "id": "C3",
    "weakest_point": "It ends on a soft, reassuring \"I will be fine\" after the ultimatum has already been delivered; the tension peaks in the first 3 seconds and then deflates into a romantic sacrifice beat.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The whispered line \"Fail, or refuse, and your husband hangs from the gallows\" is shocking, but the extreme close-up of a mouth gives no visual context in the first 3 seconds."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Leaves the question of whether she will enter the briars, but the final beat is a tender reassurance, not an unresolved peak."
    },
    "questions": [
      {"q": "Will Juliana actually crawl into the frozen thorns?", "type": "intrigue"},
      {"q": "Who is the woman whispering in the opening shot?", "type": "confusion"}
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "The opening whisper is confusing without context, though the garden scene clarifies the stakes."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The sacrificial love and Alexander’s chained helplessness are moving, but the soft ending blunts the cruelty."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "You want to see the task, but the ending lacks the urgency of a hard cut at the peak."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Handcuffs and threats only; no physical violence or injury is depicted."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Strong opening line wasted on a deflating, romantic ending that resolves the tension instead of cutting at the peak."
  }
],
  "best": "C1",
  "best_why": "C1 is the only clip that earns the stop with a context-free physical conflict in the first 3 seconds while still maintaining a clear, cruel villain peak at the end; C2 starts too mid-conversation and C3 deflates after its opening line."
}
